  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing the right to read in Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to address an alarming global trend &#x2013; the rise in numbers of children going to primary school and finishing primary school who are unable to read well enough to learn. In Rwanda, enrolment rates are now high (93%) but this rapid expansion has led to issues around quality and learning. The aim of this proposal is to ensure that during the critical early years of primary school, Rwandan children acquire strong literacy skills.  The project will do this by improving the teaching of reading, by increasing the supply of high quality local language reading materials available to read, and by doing community-based activities to engage parents and develop a popular culture of reading. As a result, over 100,000 children in primary schools in Rwanda will have an opportunity to acquire the basic literacy skills they need for on-going learning success and for life.</narrative>
  </description>
